  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 104.54 Spill",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 104.54 “Spill” means the accidental spilling, leaking, pumping, pouring, emitting, or dumping of hazardous wastes or other materials that, when spilled into or on any land or water, become hazardous wastes.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 and Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Hw 100) #12343, eff 8-14-17; (formerly Env-Hw 104.47, renumbered by #12920) (See Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Env-Hw 100); (formerly Env-Hw 104.48, renumbered by #13405) (See Revision Note #4 at chapter heading for Env-Hw 100) (formerly Env-Hw 104.52)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw100.html"
